48 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 30 0 R
/E (The Ability People \(TAP\) is a Visakhapatnam based non profit and Disabled People's Organization founded in 2007 by a spinal cord injury \(SCI\) survivor, providing inclusive, affordable, community driven rehabilitation for persons with disabilities especially in rural and tribal Andhra Pradesh. Through its Ability Rehabilitation Centre \(ARC\) in partnership with GVMC and KGH, TAP supports patients with spinal injuries, amputations, cerebral palsy, stroke, and neurological conditions. Its Community Based Rehabilitation model including Rehab on Wheels extends therapy and assistive services to remote areas. TAP also provides WHO compliant mobility aids, early intervention for children with developmental delays, and capacity building for caregivers and health workers. TAP uses digital systems to track beneficiaries, medical progress, and device usage to ensure continuity of care and long term impact.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
